# VPAA monorepo

- Apps live in `apps/`. Every directory under `apps/` is a first-class workspace app: include it in install, test, smoke, e2e, and check. Do not gitignore an app slug, negate it in `pnpm-workspace.yaml`, or skip it to make the suite pass.
- Shared code lives in `packages/`.
- Allowed DAG: `@vpaa/types` ← `@vpaa/data` ← `@vpaa/auth`. `@vpaa/semantic` and `@vpaa/config` are leaves. `@vpaa/admin` may import types, data, and auth. Apps may import all packages. Packages never import apps.
- Import `@vpaa/*` public entries only, not `src/` internals or relative hops across package roots.
- Shared versions use pnpm `catalog:`. Workspace packages use `workspace:*`.
- Default verify is `pnpm test` (unit). Then `pnpm test:smoke`. Never run full Playwright unless the user asked.
- After changing `@vpaa/data`, `@vpaa/auth`, or `@vpaa/semantic`, run `pnpm --filter <pkg>... test`.
- Graph policy: `pnpm check:deps`.
- Admin data plane lives in `@vpaa/data`; identity and membership in `@vpaa/auth`; admin UI in `@vpaa/admin`. The `@vpaa/admin` host (`src/routes`, `rayfin/`) holds only what is needed to boot and drive that UI in a browser. It is not a Fabric deployable.
- Deploy or update a Fabric app from the repo root with `pnpm up-app <slug>` (optional `--workspace "<name>"`, `--dry-run`, `--status`, `--exclude-services`). Never `npx rayfin`. Do not run `rayfin up` from the repository root. Do not use `.deployments.json` `active` as the workspace name. Pin every `@microsoft/rayfin-*` package to the same catalog version (1.36.2).
- After a substantive change in `apps/` that needs review in the live Fabric embed (UI, domain pickers, loaders, DAX, profile behavior), run `pnpm up-app <slug>` when verify is green. Do not wait to be asked. Skip tests-only, docs-only, and package-only work that is not a Fabric app. `@vpaa/admin` is not deployable.
